      "route": "/api/learning-events",
      "method": "POST",
      "previousSourceHash": "4b5d8b8a413f5b86e869c1a3",
      "issue": "#20",
      "owner": "academy-platform",
      "reason": "After the acting tenant is resolved this handler now calls requireTenantProduct(tenantContext.tenantId, \"academy\"), refusing 403 product_not_entitled when the tenant was not provisioned with Academy and 503 entitlement_unavailable when the entitlement cannot be read (multi-tenant #20, section 3.3; #429 Codex P1). PR #429 first gated only six academy routes, leaving these academy learning surfaces — the learning-events sink, the notification brain, and the trading arena and its execution and reflection writers, all carrying academy: scopes — resolving a tenant but serving Academy ungated, so an unentitled tenant kept full use of them through an omitted endpoint. The coverage test is now derived: it discovers every route that resolves a tenant from source and fails unless each either gates its product or is a listed, reasoned exemption, so this class of omission can no longer pass. Each of these operations changes only its sourceHash from the added guard; no classification, principalSource, tenantSource or existing control changed, verified against the effective manifest, which is why every entry is re-pinned rather than rewritten.",
      "replacement": {
